Read AGENTS.md before anything else — it is the full operating contract for this
repository. This folder builds websites through an 8-stage pipeline with a
zero-dependency checker; the harness you are running in has no hook enforcement,
so the contract binds you by discipline.

The floor, not a summary:
1. Any request to build/redesign/remake a website starts at stage 01 discover
   (run `node start.mjs "<name>"`, then stages/01_discover/CONTEXT.md) — ask for
   what is in the person's head (sketches, screenshots, references, brand
   colours and fonts) and for the facts, before any design or code exists.
   63 questions in stages/01_discover/questions.md; ask every BLOCKING one.
   `node checks/brief.mjs builds/<slug>` says whether discovery actually
   happened. Its output is questions to go and ask, never boxes to fill in.
2. Never invent a fact about a real business: every claim traces to a sourced
   row in builds/<slug>/facts.md.
3. Never publish a file with no traceable origin. `node assets.mjs <slug> scan`
   writes builds/<slug>/assets/MANIFEST.md; every image on a page needs a row
   with a Source and a Rights answer in the client's own words.
4. Two defaults are OFF and stay off unless brief.md says otherwise:
   `- **Motion:** none` and `- **Imagery:** client-assets-only`. Having an
   image generator is not permission; the client asking for it is.
5. The country is a file, and there is no default. Question 57 asks which
   country the business trades under; profiles/ must have it, or you research
   one (profiles/README.md) or use intl-baseline and say so. Never run the
   nearest country's law.
6. Site files go only in builds/<slug>/site/, and only after brief.md, facts.md
   and design.md exist.
7. The gate decides: `node checks/run.mjs builds/<slug>/site --facts
   builds/<slug>/facts.md`. Exit 0 ships; exit 1 does not; never --skip.
8. Stop and talk to the human at stages 01, 04, 06 and 07.

Resuming? Read builds/*/STATE.md first and continue from its Next action line.
